{
  "answers": {
    "Q1": {
      "answer": "The card asks: “Does GPU parallelism change how many of the 671 CAMELS catchments can get full Bayesian calibration instead of point optimization?” (../20261019-2345-tree/out/RESULT.md). This concerns graphics-card acceleration of parameter sampling for rainfall–runoff models; this phase measures simulation times and sampler overhead (QUESTION.md). The rule requires projected graphics-card completion below one hour and at least twentyfold acceleration over vectorized processor execution (QUESTION.md). Otherwise, the card records its predicted negative answer; completed scientific calibrations are outside this measurement phase (QUESTION.md).",
      "citations": [
        "../20261019-2345-tree/out/RESULT.md",
        "QUESTION.md"
      ]
    },
    "Q2": {
      "answer": "GR4J, a four-parameter daily rainfall–runoff model, ran through the JAX numerical library, scanning days sequentially across parallel parameter sequences called chains (run_m1.py). Measurements covered 268, 1,340 and 2,684 chains over 7,300 days, with one basin’s rainfall and evaporation repeated across chains (run_m1.py) (results_m1/out/raw/timing_rows.jsonl). Hardware comprised one NVIDIA A10 graphics card and 30 virtual processors; JAX and its compiled library were version 0.6.0, using 32-bit floating point (results_m1/out/hardware_labels.json). Each size and backend had ten timed passes at three forcing offsets after compilation warmup (results_m1/out/raw/timing_rows.jsonl). Sampler probes used 1,000 iterations for each of three seeds on each backend (results_m1/out/records/id-E5_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json).",
      "citations": [
        "run_m1.py",
        "results_m1/out/raw/timing_rows.jsonl",
        "results_m1/out/hardware_labels.json",
        "results_m1/out/records/id-E5_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json"
      ]
    },
    "Q3": {
      "answer": "The baseline was the same custom, vectorized JAX model and Metropolis sampler executed through the rented machine’s processor backend (run_m1.py). Its intended comparison concerns researchers choosing computing resources for Bayesian catchment calibration rather than point optimization (../20261019-2345-tree/out/RESULT.md). The run does not establish expert preference: its scope excludes alternative implementations, and its write-up identifies missing processor thread settings (QUESTION.md) (TAKEAWAYS_m1.md). Consequently, acceleration is relative to this implementation and machine configuration, without evidence that the processor baseline represents expert tuning (QUESTION.md) (TAKEAWAYS_m1.md).",
      "citations": [
        "run_m1.py",
        "../20261019-2345-tree/out/RESULT.md",
        "QUESTION.md",
        "TAKEAWAYS_m1.md"
      ]
    },
    "Q4": {
      "answer": "At 2,684 chains, graphics-card passes had median 88.361 milliseconds and range 88.282–88.777 milliseconds (results_m1/out/records/id-E3_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json). Processor passes had median 1,037.500 milliseconds and range 998.255–1,088.137 milliseconds at the same size (results_m1/out/records/id-E4_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json). Multiplying pass medians by 100,000 iterations and measured sampler overhead produced projected graphics-card and processor times of 2.463 and 29.841 hours (results_m1/out/records/id-E5_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json). Their ratio, 12.115, misses the required twentyfold acceleration, while projected graphics-card completion exceeds the one-hour limit (results_m1/out/records/id-E5_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json). Full-run uncertainty intervals were not recorded; the separate six-hour planning gate was met (results_m1/out/records/id-E5_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json) (results_m1/out/records/id-E6_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json).",
      "citations": [
        "results_m1/out/records/id-E3_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json",
        "results_m1/out/records/id-E4_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json",
        "results_m1/out/records/id-E5_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json",
        "results_m1/out/records/id-E6_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json"
      ]
    },
    "Q5": {
      "answer": "On the 59-day example, graphics-card and processor runs achieved Nash–Sutcliffe efficiency scores of 0.494775 and 0.494774, respectively (results_m1/out/records/id-E2_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json). This flow-fit score was compared with published 0.495, allowing an absolute difference of 0.02 (results_m1/out/records/id-E2_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json). Additional cases reproduced published scores 0.336 and 0.570 as approximately 0.335984 and 0.569931 on both backends, within the same tolerance (results_m1/out/records/id-I2_kind-control_tag-m1.json). Independent airGR reference code never ran, so daily-flow agreement below one percent mean absolute relative error remained unchecked (results_m1/out/records/id-E2_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json). Planted zero-rain, response-weight and water-balance checks passed their recorded thresholds using the scalar model implementation (results_m1/out/records/id-I2_kind-control_tag-m1.json) (run_m1.py).",
      "citations": [
        "results_m1/out/records/id-E2_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json",
        "results_m1/out/records/id-I2_kind-control_tag-m1.json",
        "run_m1.py"
      ]
    },
    "Q6": {
      "answer": "Forecasts were sealed before measurement (RUN.md) (SEALED_PREDICTIONS.md). For 2,684 chains, graphics-card time 88.36 milliseconds held the predicted 20–200 range (results_m1/out/records/id-E3_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json) (SEALED_PREDICTIONS.md). Acceleration was 12.11-fold, contradicting the below-five forecast; the twentyfold event did not occur (results_m1/out/records/id-E5_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json) (SEALED_PREDICTIONS.md). Overhead 1.0035 missed the 1.5–3 interval but remained below four; projected 2.46 hours contradicted above-six expectations (results_m1/out/records/id-E5_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json) (SEALED_PREDICTIONS.md). The negative decision held; throughput from 268 to 2,684 chains increased 8.76-fold, within the predicted band (results_m1/out/records/id-E5_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json) (results_m1/out/records/id-E7_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json) (SEALED_PREDICTIONS.md). First-launch completion failed, and independent reproduction remained unresolved (out/launch1/results_m1/out/RUN_VALID.json) (results_m1/out/records/id-E1_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json). The scorer counted the flow-agreement forecast as held despite its untested daily-flow component (out/PREDICTIONS_SCORED.md).",
      "citations": [
        "RUN.md",
        "SEALED_PREDICTIONS.md",
        "results_m1/out/records/id-E3_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json",
        "results_m1/out/records/id-E5_kind-endpoint_tag-m1.json",
